# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings for the files where they matter.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A blanket "* text=auto" would renormalise the whole
# repository on the next checkout, producing a large and confusing diff to fix
# a problem that affects a handful of files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Windows script files need CRLF. A batch file with Unix line endings can
# misbehave on Windows in ways that are hard to diagnose: `goto` can fail to
# find a label and multi line `if` blocks can break, with no message saying
# why. These files are authored on Linux, so the rule is stated rather than
# left to chance.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Compiled by Inno Setup, which is Windows only.
*.iss  text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on a Windows checkout, or bash refuses to
# run them.
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Never convert these.
*.exe  binary
*.dcm  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ico  binary
